{
  "id": "ss.pickup.coin",
  "name": "Jelly bead",
  "description": "The currency, JELLY: a bead of royal jelly, the food the hive raises its queens on, and the one thing it makes that the expedition trades in. Drawn as a droplet sitting on its round end, a point up and a full belly, because that silhouette is the one no other pickup has: the pulp is a lobed lump, the healing sac (`ss.pickup.food`) a round body with a stem, and the brood cell a stretched hexagon. This used to be a plate of shell, the other hexagon on the floor, which said nothing about jelly. Translucent amber in three values and no gradient, since the bake flattens one: an amber skin where the drop is thickest, gold where the light comes through and pools in the belly, and two pale marks, the shine on the upper shoulder where the light lands and the light caught along the inside of the belly. It does not glow. There is no halo and no pink, and its brightest marks sit at its edges, where reflected light sits, because in this world only the hive's organs give off light. Gold-warm, as the currency always was, so it still reads as currency at a glance. Every part hangs from the point the bead rests on, which is the pivot `wobble` rocks it about. The bead darkens at its foot where it sits, and carries a second, smaller sparkle on its shade side.",
  "tags": ["pickup"],
  "size": [16, 16],
